"site-nav-button examples" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		Site nav button
		<header>A site nav button shows or hides the side navigation of the page layout around it:  its icons only and back on a wide page, slid in and out on a narrow one.</>
	</>

	<section label="Types">
		<section label="In a top bar" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "In a top bar" description="In the start of a page layout's top bar, it's one of the bar's items, its icon `columns`.  On a wide layout a press shows only the drawer's icons, or all of it again;  on a narrow one it slides the drawer in and out.">
				<ui-page-layout style="min-height: 12em">
					<app-menu slot="menu">
						<site-nav-button slot="start" />
						<item slot="start">My site</>
					</>
					<site-nav slot="drawer" appearance="nav" current="#home" pages="\[{ \"title\": \"Home\", \"href\": \"#home\", \"icon\": \"home\" }, { \"title\": \"Films\", \"href\": \"#films\", \"icon\": \"film\" }]" />
					<text paragraph>Press the button:  the drawer shows only its icons, or all of it again.</>
				</>
			</example>
		</>
	</>
